<title>SOUTH KOREA: BOK sells dollars in forward trading - traders.</title>
<headline>BOK sells dollars in forward trading - traders.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The central Bank of Korea (BOK) sold dollars in early forward trading to support the won, traders said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The BOK was observed selling $20 million in three-month forward trading at he 868.50 won level, and another $20 million in six-month forward trading at $881.00, they said.</p>
<p>The BOK has refused to comment on interventions in the market.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5644</p>
